  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 0.5 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}1.5 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0.2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "- $P$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $3$ rows and $2$ columns, so it's a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $S$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $2$ rows and $2$ columns, so it is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $T$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $5$ rows and $5$ columns, so it is a $5\\times 5$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, only $S$ and $T$ are square matrices.",
